{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c987eab9-ba63-4425-9c8e-ad482b906b60","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b565442ba0c2e809","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-0v1zpg0d/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers administrator-facing idle and stale resource reporting in\nthe RHOAI web console. Cluster administrators get a per-project view of idle\nworkbenches (with last activity, owner, and reserved resources) and stale\npipeline runs (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained\nartifacts), plus CSV export of either report. The data is sourced from\ncapabilities that already exist in the platform — the notebook controller's\nlast-activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata — so all\ncode changes land in the web console; no changes are made to the notebook\ncontroller or the pipelines component.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A per-project idle-workbench report in the web console showing, for each\n  workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n  tracking), owner, and reserved resources.\n- A stale pipeline-run report in the web console showing completed runs older\n  than a configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from\n  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- A configurable staleness age threshold for the pipeline-run report.\n- CSV export of either report, containing the same columns as the on-screen\n  report.\n- Validation that reported values reconcile with the upstream data sources\n  (notebook controller activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run\n  metadata) — these components keep working unchanged; correctness of the\n  reports against them is part of this epic's deliverable.\n- Read-only reporting only. Automated reclamation or deletion of idle\n  resources and cost/chargeback calculations are out of scope and must not be\n  introduced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches with differing last-activity times,\n  the console renders a per-project idle-workbench report listing each\n  workbench's last activity, owner, and reserved resources.\n- The idle-workbench report's last-activity values reconcile with the\n  notebook controller's activity tracking for the same workbenches\n  (spot-checked against the source data).\n- Given completed pipeline runs of varying age, the stale pipeline-run report\n  lists exactly the completed runs older than the configured age, together\n  with their retained artifacts, and its values reconcile with Kubeflow\n  Pipelines run completion metadata.\n- The staleness age threshold is configurable, and changing it changes which\n  runs appear in the stale pipeline-run report.\n- Either report can be exported as CSV, and the exported file contains the\n  same rows and columns as the on-screen report and opens correctly in\n  standard spreadsheet tools.\n- The reports expose no reclamation, deletion, or cost-calculation actions\n  (read-only; out-of-scope guard).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — Primary. The per-project idle-workbench report (last\n  activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's\n  activity tracking.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Primary. The stale pipeline-run report (completed runs\n  older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from\n  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- **HLR-3 (P2)** — Bundled. CSV export of either report shares the same\n  reporting UI surface, data structures, and query paths as the P1 reports;\n  it is not separately schedulable and is delivered inside this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34631,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92e85