ion steps are\n  published in the RHOAI documentation set.\n- Every statement about report contents, configuration, and behavior is\n  validated against the shipped implementation and matches it (accuracy\n  pass).\n- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation by the\n  engineering team that built the reporting capability, and review feedback\n  is addressed.\n- The documentation states that the reports are read-only and does not\n  describe reclamation, deletion, or cost features that do not exist.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P2)** — Primary. Documentation explains the reports and safe\n  reclamation steps.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35776,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92e85813c1eb1fb4","agent_id":"a86ceb0064c274d4d","session_id":"dad7cdcd-70eb-4422-b2ee-b16caf3527cf","uuid":"606a2729-210c-4ccc-925a-3941ebea61f7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:00:48.921Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016 into epics"}
