2)\n40\t\n41\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P1) are primary coverage in\n42\tRHAISTRAT-9016-E001; HLR-4 (P2) is primary coverage in RHAISTRAT-9016-E002;\n43\tHLR-3 (P2, CSV export) is bundled into E001 with an explicit, justified entry in\n44\tthe traceability matrix. The bundling call is sound: CSV export is a thin\n45\tserialization increment over the same report rows, columns, and query paths the\n46\tP1 reports already produce — splitting it would rebuild the same surface, and\n47\tthe strategy's problem statement asks for one reporting surface. Priority\n48\tinheritance: E001 blocks no P0 work (its only dependent is the docs epic, which\n49\tis exempt); E002's P2 correctly derives from the strategy's `Normal` priority\n50\tvia the docs-authoring exception, not from inheritance. No priority inversions.\n51\tTraceability matrix present in the summary and per-epic HLR Traceability\n52\tsections exist in both epic bodies.\n53\t\n54\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n55\t\n56\tSingle edge E001 → E002 (Rule 11, docs last), present in both the mermaid\n57\tdiagram (dependency → dependent direction, correct convention) and E002's\n58\tfrontmatter `dependencies`. E001 has no dependencies, matching the diagram. No\n59\tcircular dependencies, no invalid edges, no branch files, no konflux-onboarding\n60\tor license epics (so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not in play). Critical path\n61\tlength 2 matches the S-strategy heuristic (1-2). Cross-check for uncaptured\n62\tdata dependencies: E001 consumes notebook-controller activity data and KFP run\n63\tmetadata from passive components that need no code changes (correctly no epics,\n64\tno edges); E002's only input is E001's shipped implementation, which is the\n65\texisting edge. No missing edges found in epic content.\n66\t\n67\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n68\t\n69\tE001: component Dashboard, team RHOAI Dashboard — matches the owning team in\n70\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`. E002:\n71\tcomponent Documentation (in the canonical `.context/rhai-components.txt` list),\n72\tteam RHOAI Documentation — inferred in the absence of a Documentation context\n73\tfile, and explicitly flagged as an assumption in the summary's Health Warnings\n74\trather than silently asserted. Code implementation and documentation authoring\n75\tare correctly separated into different epics (no work-product type mixing). No\n76\tscope duplication between the two epics. Both epics are within the ~2-week\n77\tguideline (two report views plus export over one surface; one documentation\n78\ttopic set), and the summary records the size assessment.\n79\t\n80\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n81\t\n82\tNo Investigation epics — justified: the strategy declares \"Open Questions:\n83\tNone\" and contains no conditional ADRs, pending reviews, or risks; the\n84\tdecomposition explicitly reasoned through the one candidate unknown (console\n85\treadability of notebook-controller activity data) and handled it as a\n86\tvalidation acceptance criterion plus a named health warning with a concrete\n87\tfallback (an additional Notebooks-component epic), which is a defensible\n88\tjudgment call given the strategy's premise. Both epics are Implementation and\n89\tproduce concrete artifacts (shipped console reports; published documentation\n90\ttopics). No `gated_by` fields are set and no epic lists an Investigation\n91\tdependency, so the gating-metadata checks are vacuously satisfied.\n92\t\n93\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n94\t\n95\tBoth epics are Implementation type and correctly carry `ai_signals` (not\n96\t`investigation_signals`); both ai-signals files exist with per-signal rationales.\n97\tE001's values check out against the strategy and the context files:\n98\tpattern_precedent/existing_foundation (console already renders per-project\n99\tworkbench and pipeline-run lists per dashboard.md), open_questions (strategy\n100\tdeclares none), repo_access (public upstream ope