{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4024a9101f8ab36","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers administrator-facing idle and stale resource reporting in\n34\tthe RHOAI web console. Cluster administrators get a per-project view of idle\n35\tworkbenches (with last activity, owner, and reserved resources) and stale\n36\tpipeline runs (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained\n37\tartifacts), plus CSV export of either report. The data is sourced from\n38\tcapabilities that already exist in the platform — the notebook controller's\n39\tlast-activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata — so all\n40\tcode changes land in the web console; no changes are made to the notebook\n41\tcontroller or the pipelines component.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- A per-project idle-workbench report in the web console showing, for each\n46\t  workbench: last activity (sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n47\t  tracking), owner, and reserved resources.\n48\t- A stale pipeline-run report in the web console showing completed runs older\n49\t  than a configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from\n50\t  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n51\t- A configurable staleness age threshold for the pipeline-run report.\n52\t- CSV export of either report, containing the same columns as the on-screen\n53\t  report.\n54\t- Validation that reported values reconcile with the upstream data sources\n55\t  (notebook controller activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines run\n56\t  metadata) — these components keep working unchanged; correctness of the\n57\t  reports against them is part of this epic's deliverable.\n58\t- Read-only reporting only. Automated reclamation or deletion of idle\n59\t  resources and cost/chargeback calculations are out of scope and must not be\n60\t  introduced.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given a project containing workbenches with differing last-activity times,\n65\t  the console renders a per-project idle-workbench report listing each\n66\t  workbench's last activity, owner, and reserved resources.\n67\t- The idle-workbench report's last-activity values reconcile with the\n68\t  notebook controller's activity tracking for the same workbenches\n69\t  (spot-checked against the source data).\n70\t- Given completed pipeline runs of varying age, the stale pipeline-run report\n71\t  lists exactly the completed runs older than the configured age, together\n72\t  with their retained artifacts, and its values reconcile with Kubeflow\n73\t  Pipelines run completion metadata.\n74\t- The staleness age threshold is configurable, and changing it changes which\n75\t  runs appear in the stale pipeline-run report.\n76\t- Either report can be exported as CSV, and the exported file contains the\n77\t  same rows and columns as the on-screen report and opens correctly in\n78\t  standard spreadsheet tools.\n79\t- The reports expose no reclamation, deletion, or cost-calculation actions\n80\t  (read-only; out-of-scope guard).\n81\t\n82\t## HLR Traceability\n83\t\n84\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — Primary. The per-project idle-workbench report (last\n85\t  activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's\n86\t  activity tracking.\n87\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — Primary. The stale pipeline-run report (completed runs\n88\t  older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from\n89\t  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n90\t- **HLR-3 (P2)** — Bundled. CSV export of either report shares the same\n91\t  reporting UI surface, data structures, and query paths as the P1 reports;\n92\t  it is not separately schedulable and is delivered inside this epic.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8720d242dadc1dd4","agent_id":"a0673c743dee297d0","session_id":"dad7cdcd-70eb-4422-b2ee-b16caf3527cf","uuid":"b9e7abd3-26d4-4aeb-977f-dc2ed0d9b330","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:05:03.456Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4024a9101f8ab36","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
