{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab2d07c0e0b3c7b1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\ttitle: Idle resource reporting in the web console\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Normal\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\tlinks: []\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## Problem Statement\n12\t\n13\tCluster administrators cannot see which resources are sitting idle: workbenches\n14\tnobody has touched in weeks keep their volumes and reservations, and old\n15\tpipeline runs accumulate storage. Admins ask for a single report in the RHOAI\n16\tweb console showing idle and stale resources per project so they can reclaim\n17\tcapacity with confidence. The notebook controller already tracks last-activity\n18\ttimestamps, and Kubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata — the data\n19\texists; it is just not surfaced anywhere.\n20\t\n21\t## High-Level Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n24\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n25\t| HLR-1 | P1 | The web console shows a per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources), sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking. |\n26\t| HLR-2 | P1 | The web console shows a stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts), sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata. |\n27\t| HLR-3 | P2 | Administrators can export either report as CSV. |\n28\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps. |\n29\t\n30\t## Affected Components\n31\t\n32\t- RHOAI web console\n33\t- Notebook controller\n34\t- Kubeflow Pipelines\n35\t\n36\t## Out of Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources\n39\t- Cost/chargeback calculations\n40\t\n41\t## Open Questions\n42\t\n43\tNone.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8720d242dadc1dd4","agent_id":"a0673c743dee297d0","session_id":"dad7cdcd-70eb-4422-b2ee-b16caf3527cf","uuid":"bb4636a