e threshold, how to\n52\t  change it, and how retained artifacts are shown.\n53\t- Exporting either report as CSV and working with the exported data.\n54\t- Safe reclamation steps: what an administrator should verify before stopping\n55\t  or removing an idle workbench or deleting a stale run and its artifacts,\n56\t  including cautions about data that is still needed.\n57\t- Explicit statement of limitations: the reports are read-only; automated\n58\t  reclamation and cost/chargeback are not provided.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Documentation topics covering the reports, their data sources, the\n63\t  configurable staleness age, CSV export, and safe reclamation steps are\n64\t  published in the RHOAI documentation set.\n65\t- Every statement about report contents, configuration, and behavior is\n66\t  validated against the shipped implementation and matches it (accuracy\n67\t  pass).\n68\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation by the\n69\t  engineering team that built the reporting capability, and review feedback\n70\t  is addressed.\n71\t- The documentation states that the reports are read-only and does not\n72\t  describe reclamation, deletion, or cost features that do not exist.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-4 (P2)** — Primary. Documentation explains the reports and safe\n77\t  reclamation steps.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81b82d24186b858b","agent_id":"a452add63e5566b03","session_id":"dad7cdcd-70eb-4422-b2ee-b16caf3527cf","uuid":"4484b85a-0998-4c45-a415-c559b6924989","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:07:18.945Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac67f285b0c53aa6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
